t: chat, logs, timelines" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#5F667A;fontSize=8.5;fontFamily=Helvetica" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="548" y="428" width="246" height="14" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="t-68" value="cost: needs a tie-breaker" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#D97706;fontSize=8.5;fontFamily=Helvetica" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="548" y="444" width="246" height="14" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b-69" value="The test for a fake cursor: can the client compute the next one? &lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Courier New&quot;&gt;cursor = last + pageSize&lt;/span&gt; is an offset wearing a cursor’s name — same drift, same O(N) scan." style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FEF6E7;strokeColor=#D97706;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#6B3A05;fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;shadow=0" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="472" width="772" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b-70" value="A real cursor is opaque and minted by the server, because it encodes the sort key it is anchored to. If you can do arithmetic on it, nothing was fixed — the parameter was just renamed." style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FEF6E7;strokeColor=#D97706;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#6B3A05;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;shadow=0" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="528" width="772" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>